{
  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: multimodal, multiprofile, scgpt, resnet50, avgpool, concat → acc 0.512), the most critical uncertainty is whether the multimodal fusion is actually contributing value or whether the low accuracy reflects a fundamental limitation of the setup. config_018 (rna_only, multiprofile, scgpt, avgpool) is the cleanest single-factor comparison to config_001: it removes only the image modality and fusion while holding the RNA encoder (scgpt), profile setting (multiprofile), and aggregation (avgpool) constant. If RNA-only performs comparably to 0.512, it suggests the image modality or fusion strategy is not adding signal, redirecting effort toward better unimodal representations or fusion design. If RNA-only is substantially worse, it confirms the image contributes meaningful information and justifies further multimodal exploration. Under a tight budget, establishing whether the core multimodal premise is valid before investing in more complex multimodal variants (transformer aggregation, weighted fusion, ViT encoders) is the highest-information-value next step."
}

